The first method subsets the data into four groups and finds the mean of each group.  The second method uses a linear model without an intercept to estimate mean shapes, which are the coefficients.  There are other ways (using the aggregate function after making data into a matrix is another good one) but either of these are pretty efficient, using geomorph functions.

